  "summary": "@keyv/compress-lz4 LZ4 compression adapter — base64/Buffer usage consistent with codec, no installer-harm evidence",
  "details": "Package is an LZ4 compression adapter for the keyv key-value store. The dist bundles (dist/index.cjs and dist/index.mjs) contain Buffer.from(..., 'base64')/.toString() calls, which is the expected shape for a compression/serialization codec that encodes and decodes binary payloads. No lifecycle scripts fetching remote content, no environment-variable or credential-path reads, no network exfiltration destinations, and no eval/exec of decoded content are present. The pattern-match on Buffer.from + base64 alone does not indicate installer-side harm.",
